         <div type="bio">
            <p>French journalist and government official. In preparation for the “séance” to promote <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Ulysses</name> on 7 December 1921, the then young Benoist-Méchin was engaged to translate into French the end of “Penelope”. He later became a journalist and editor and, in the late 1930s and during WWII, an avid collaborationist, active in the Vichy government. Benoist-Méchin was the source for JJ’s purported quotation that he “put in so many enigmas and puzzles that it will keep the professors busy for centuries” (<name type="work">JJ</name> 521), but the accuracy of his recollection has been disputed. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
